---
source: crates/pgls_workspace/tests/template_formatting.rs
---
-- a directive after a name can't be read, like the alias `%s` without `as`: the statement stays
-- as written. Found by the fuzzer: to Go, the `%t` of `FROM%tenk1` is a directive, so the
-- name `FROM%tenk1` follows `four`, and the formatter wrote `cast(FROM%tenk1 as four)`
select   a %s from t;
select ten, four FROM%tenk1 where unique2 < 10;
select a as %s from t;

---
diagnostics:
  `%s`: A template placeholder directly after `a` can't be read: write `AS` before an alias; a placeholder can stand for a name or a value, not a SQL clause.
  `FROM%tenk1`: A template placeholder directly after `four` can't be read: write `AS` before an alias; a placeholder can stand for a name or a value, not a SQL clause.
